cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NexusQC: Agentic Quantum Chemistry Engine"
abstract: >-
  A conversational agent for computational chemistry. It resolves molecules
  from names, SMILES or sketches, elicits missing calculation parameters
  instead of guessing them, and runs quantum chemistry jobs across PySCF,
  ORCA and BAGEL behind a human approval gate, with results visualised in the
  browser and a retrieval-augmented knowledge base for follow-up questions.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dakshitha-a/NexusQC"
authors:
  - given-names: Dakshitha
    family-names: Abeygunewardane
    email: dma@temple.edu
    affiliation: "Matsika Group, Temple University"
keywords:
  - computational chemistry
  - quantum chemistry
  - CASSCF
  - CASPT2
  - large language model
  - agent
  - PySCF
  - ORCA
  - BAGEL
message: >-
  If you use NexusQC in your research, please cite it using the metadata in
  this file. Please also cite the quantum chemistry program that actually
  performed your calculation (PySCF, ORCA or BAGEL) -- NexusQC orchestrates
  those programs, it does not implement the underlying methods.

  Affiliation at the time of project creation: Matsika Group, Temple
  University. Principal investigator: Spiridoula Matsika
  (smatsika@temple.edu). Coded with Claude Code (Model: Opus).
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
